  "term": "activity deprivation",
  "definition": "Activity deprivation is the loss or experimental blocking of neurons’ normal spontaneous activity. In the supplied source, it refers to prolonged blockade of neuronal activity, which is linked to slow neurodegeneration and cell death.",
